GENERATED_FROM: brainstack-universal (the Claude Code plugin at
github.com/UseBrainstack/brainstack-claude), re-shaped for the Codex plugin
system used by the ChatGPT desktop app (Codex + ChatGPT-work).

Same `bsb` binaries (Mac universal Mach-O + Windows PE), byte-identical copies of
the brainstack-universal runtime — the Brainstack MCP connector (`bsb connect`)
in one native binary, no Node. OAuth token at ~/.brainstack/token.json.

2026-09-11: local capture hooks were RETIRED. Apps are moving to cloud/VM
execution, so a local hook shipping a transcript is unreliable; capture is now
MCP-driven filing over the connector (private by default), and deterministic
auto-capture is a Compliance-API feature. The plugin no longer ships hooks.json
and the plugin manifest no longer declares hooks — it's connector-only.

Codex plugin scaffold specifics:
  - Marketplace manifest at .agents/plugins/marketplace.json (Codex schema:
    interface.displayName; plugins[].source={source,path};
    policy={installation,authentication,products:["CODEX"]}; category).
  - Plugin manifest at plugins/brainstack/.codex-plugin/plugin.json with the
    Codex `interface` block; mcpServers -> ./.mcp.json.
  - .mcp.json uses a relative stdio command (./runtime/bsb + cwd:".") instead of
    the ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} variable.
  - The one-time importer (import-old-chats.sh/.ps1) uses `bsb login` to sign in
    and `bsb ingest` to upload each transcript, then cleans itself up.

Connector endpoint unchanged: https://usebrainstack.com/mcp
